{"name":"Loft Light","hex":"#dccab7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"loft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Air, the air; the sky, the heavens.","An attic or similar space (often used for storage) in the roof of a house or other building.\nSuch an attic used as an atelier."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To propel high into the air.","To fly or travel through the air, as though propelled"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loft"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loft","blocks":[{"text":"A loft is a building's upper storey or elevated area in a room directly under the roof, or just an attic: a storage space under the roof usually accessed by a ladder. A loft apartment refers to large adaptable open space, often converted for residential use from some other use, often light industrial."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/400SGreenLoft.jpg/330px-400SGreenLoft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loft","wikidata":"Q620861"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thu